              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "bvwinemaker"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made some additions, and hopefully the GKids will love them! Added 20 ozs. Of Pineapple tidbits and 2/3 C. Chopped Almonds and 1/2 C. Rice Krispies! At 12 minutes, out of the oven, they had a great Stand-Up appearance, and I believe Presentation is Key! Oh, and of course, I prayed and added full Cup Love",
            "datePublished": "2020-09-12T14:32:55.840Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "heatherljc"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I baked the first 6 to see how they taste. I couldn't taste the pineapple or coconut so I added more pineapple in and coconut sprinkled on top with sugar for the second test. Upon tasting them I added more pineapple, coconut and dried cranberries. Then I could taste the pineapple a little more and I just love cranberries. I wont make this recipe again but thanks for sharing.",
            "datePublished": "2019-06-23T02:33:08.927Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "2"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Cricket"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These are very cake-like, and bland. They would be great for whoopie pies perhaps, but the pineapple and coconut are lost in dough. Not something I would do again, but it did sound good.",
            "datePublished": "2017-08-12T20:18:36.007Z"
